13. What makes this app genuinely better than existing tools

Your wedge is not “project management.”

Your wedge is:

AI-native product execution for builders who move from idea to shipped software using GitHub.

That means your differentiation is:

idea-to-shipping continuity
AI context packs
Codex + Claude orchestration
GitHub-aware execution
improvement suggestions
founder-centric UX
less clutter than enterprise tools

That’s strong.

14. Biggest mistakes to avoid
Don’t do this
Too many required fields up front
Overly enterprise language
Generic task app UX
Too many disconnected modules
No opinionated stages
No “next best action”
Weak GitHub integration
Weak AI handoff structure
Overusing vector search where relational structure is enough
Letting AI write directly everywhere without permission controls
Also don’t
Build for teams first
Copy Jira
Copy Notion databases blindly
Add every productivity gimmick
Treat “ideas” and “execution” as separate products
15. My strongest recommendation for the product shape

Build it around these 5 screens first:

1. Home

The command center.

2. Ideas

Capture, score, enrich, and convert to project.

3. Project workspace

Overview, roadmap, docs, GitHub, AI actions.

4. Execution

Tasks, blockers, milestones, next actions.

5. GitHub/PR cockpit

PRs, checks, reviews, merge readiness, AI review.

If those 5 are excellent, the whole product works.

16. Best internal mantra for building it

Every object in the system should answer:

What is it?
Why does it matter?
What’s the next step?
What is blocking it?
What changed recently?
What should AI do with it?
What should I do with it?

If a screen does not answer those, it’s noise.

17. Final product definition in one sentence

A founder-grade AI-native operating system for turning ideas into shipped products, with roadmap planning, execution control, GitHub integration, and Codex/Claude-powered delivery loops.
